## Why This Is Asked
Tests a privacy-critical, cross-service E2E flow—data erasure across region boundaries, backups, and auditability. It probes data isolation, idempotency, and outage resilience in a realistic multi-service setup.

## Key Concepts
- Privacy-by-design data deletion across microservices
- Cross-region data isolation and leakage prevention
- Idempotent delete semantics
- Deterministic testing via ETL mocks
- End-to-end audit trails and backup purge checks

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-test scaffold for Cypress/Playwright
describe('Delete My Data E2E', () => {
  it('erases tenant data across services and purges backups on SLA', async () => {
    await loginAsUser('regionA');
    await triggerDeleteRequest();
    await verifyServiceDeletion('Auth');
    await verifyServiceDeletion('CRM');
    await verifyServiceDeletion('Analytics');
    await verifyServicePurgeBackups();
    // idempotency
    await triggerDeleteRequest();
    await verifyNoOp(),
  });
});
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests at the beginner level often miss realistic offline scenarios and deterministic retries. This question probes practical E2E thinking: isolation, network control, and idempotent submission.

## Key Concepts

- End-to-end orchestration of multi-step flows
- Auto-save timing and state persistence (e.g., localStorage/IndexedDB)
- Offline/online transition handling and reconciling state
- Mocking external APIs (identity) for determinism
- Ensuring single, idempotent final submit

## Code Example

```javascript
// Playwright sketch (context-level offline, data isolation, mocked API)
const context = await browser.newContext({ storageState: 'test-user.json' });
const page = await context.newPage();
await context.setOffline(true);
await page.goto('https://finapp/onboarding');
// perform step interactions, wait for auto-save marker, then go online
await context.setOffline(false);
// verify single submit
```

